      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Trajector\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/48/1914_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Trajector:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>TakeWalker wrote:</b>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I was surprised by how brief this was, but I guess two-thirds of the content was already covered in previous episodes. &lt;.&lt; Which is odd, since, y’know, title of this one and all…</p>\n<p>Still a good story. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n</blockquote>\n</div>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Man, I wish I had listened to the Ra and Ennead episodes right before this one, because I think I forgot everything relevant! Maybe I’ll take a look at the wiki later to see if I can remind myself of the whole story.</p>\n<p>This kind of slipped through as an aside: Christopher said that&nbsp;<em>The History of Sentinel Comics</em>&nbsp;would be “part of” the Kickstarter for the RPG. I hope it’ll be purchase-able as a standalone, too!</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yeah, given how long it had been since the Ra and Ennead episodes, I wouldn’t have minded this being a comprehensive overview of that whole storyline in greater detail than before, but there was still some decent revelations, particularly about Ra and Fanatic.</p>",
